  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is very weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant signal source. The key uncertainty is whether the linear PCA representation is suboptimal and whether a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) can capture richer biological structure. This experiment (config_004: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) isolates the RNA encoder effect by changing only the encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while keeping model setting and profile setting identical to config_001. This is the best use of the next slot because: (1) improving the dominant modality is the highest-leverage move, (2) it provides a clean single-variable comparison to attribute any gain/loss to the encoder, (3) the result directly informs which RNA encoder to pair with multimodal fusion in later experiments, and (4) with 7 experiments remaining, establishing the best RNA backbone early maximizes the value of subsequent multimodal tests."
}

